 			The framerate-independent update speed when representing dynamic object lighting from [LightmapProbe]s. Higher values make dynamic object lighting update faster. Higher values can prevent fast-moving objects from having "outdated" indirect lighting displayed on them, at the cost of possible flickering when an object moves from a bright area to a shaded area.
 			[b]Note:[/b] This property is only read when the project starts. To adjust the BVH build quality at runtime, use [method RenderingServer.lightmap_set_probe_capture_update_speed].
 		</member>
+		<member name="rendering/lights_and_shadows/contact_shadow/enabled" type="bool" setter="" getter="" default="false">
+			If [code]true[/code], screen-space contact shadows are enabled. These catch small-scale shadows that shadow maps miss, such as foliage, crevices, and the contact points where objects meet surfaces. Contact shadows are also cast by objects that have their [member GeometryInstance3D.cast_shadow] property set to [constant GeometryInstance3D.SHADOW_CASTING_SETTING_OFF], which can be useful for performance reasons.
+			[b]Note:[/b] Only objects visible on screen can cast screen-space contact shadows. Objects outside the viewport, occluded by other geometry, or using the [member GeometryInstance3D.cast_shadow] property set to [constant GeometryInstance3D.SHADOW_CASTING_SETTING_SHADOWS_ONLY] will not contribute.
+			[b]Note:[/b] Screen-space contact shadows are only supported in the Forward+ renderer, not Mobile or Compatibility.
+			[b]Note:[/b] Screen-space contact shadows only affect [DirectionalLight3D] nodes that have shadows enabled. The [DirectionalLight3D] node must also have [member Light3D.shadow_contact_shadows_allow] set to [code]true[/code].
+		</member>
+		<member name="rendering/lights_and_shadows/contact_shadow/shadow_length" type="int" setter="" getter="" default="1">
+			Controls the maximum distance contact shadows can be cast from their caster. Higher settings sample further along the shadow ray, at a moderate performance cost. Note that the effective maximum distance depends on the distance between the camera and object, as well as the 3D rendering resolution (determined by the viewport resolution multiplied by [member rendering/scaling_3d/scale]).
+		</member>
+		<member name="rendering/lights_and_shadows/contact_shadow/surface_thickness" type="float" setter="" getter="" default="0.01">
+			The assumed depth thickness of surfaces, as a fraction of the depth range. A larger value widens the depth interval in which an occluder is considered to block light, which can fill in gaps in thin geometry but may also cause shadows to bleed through surfaces if set too high.
+		</member>
 		<member name="rendering/lights_and_shadows/directional_shadow/16_bits" type="bool" setter="" getter="" default="true">
 			Use 16 bits for the directional shadow depth map. Enabling this results in shadows having less precision and may result in shadow acne, but can lead to performance improvements on some devices.
 		</member>
